  "details": "Download speed does not appear to be the problem. The issue seems to occur during avatar initialization.\n\nIf I enter a crowded instance while allowing many avatars to appear normally, SteamVR can crash during the loading/initialization burst.\n\nHowever, if I initially limit shown avatars, wait for them to fully initialize, then progressively increase the shown-avatar count, the same system can tolerate the resulting load. It may stutter heavily, but it recovers instead of crashing.\n\nThis suggests that limiting concurrent avatar initialization may improve stability on systems under VRAM/resource pressure.\n\nA setting such as Maximum Concurrent Avatar Initializations: 1 / 2 / Auto would allow users to trade loading speed for stability.",
